Description:
	Administration Roles and ACL section body.

	Lists every role with its family, what it is for, how many permissions it carries and how many
	people hold it. Manage opens the permission editor for one role; the permissions themselves are
	never edited from this table.

	Column widths are declared here rather than in a header model because this list is not
	paginated: there are a few dozen roles and they are all shown. The proportions follow the same
	convention as every paginated table - one row is one line, the widest column is the one carrying
	prose, and anything too long for its column is truncated with its full text in a tooltip.

	The role key sits under the role name in the same cell. The table system renders a secondary line
	inline behind a separator, so it costs no second row.

	WARNING: a template comment is not a safe place to document syntax. F3 parses its own tags inside
	comments, so a tag written out as a usage example becomes a real tag in the compiled template.
	Keep every comment plain prose: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens and
	no code.
Changelog:
	2026/09/07 18:05 SAST
	- Given column widths and tooltips, and the create form moved into a modal: the Role column was
		squashed to a few characters by an untamed Description column, and the create form was a
		popover inside a duplicate page heading.
